How to setup a django project

Create a requirements.txt file with the following content:
`
django
djangorestframework
environs
asgiref
tzdata
django-extensions
`

Then run the following command to install the dependencies:
`pip install -r requirements.txt`

Next, create a new Django project by running the following command:

`django-admin startproject myproject`

This will create a new directory called myproject with the necessary files and folders for a Django project. You can navigate into the project directory using:cd myproject
To start the development server, run the following command:
`python manage.py runserver`
This will start the server and you can access your Django project by opening a web browser and going to http://

